# CoreUI icon manifest — the vendor icons compiled into Styles/CoreIcons.axaml.
#
# Source: https://github.com/coreui/coreui-icons — CoreUI Icons Free.
# Icons are CC BY 4.0 (attribution required, see Docs/ThirdPartyNotices.md);
# brand marks (cib-*) are CC0 but remain trademarks of their owners.
# Regenerate after editing:  python3 Scripts/generate-coreui-icons.py
#
# Syntax
#   <slug>                       free icon  svg/free/cil-<slug>.svg   -> CoreIcon<PascalSlug>
#   brand:<slug>                 brand icon svg/brand/cib-<slug>.svg  -> CoreIcon<PascalSlug>
#   <Key> = <slug> + plus@<span>,<cx>,<cy>
#                                composite; a plus of <span> units, drawn at CoreUI's own stroke
#                                weight, is centred at (cx, cy) on the icon's canvas and merged
#                                into the base as one nonzero-fill geometry.  Place it inside the
#                                base's hollow interior — the two shapes share a colour, so an
#                                overlap just fuses them.
#
# Keep this list to icons the app actually uses: every entry becomes a StreamGeometry that
# is constructed when the resource dictionary loads.

